WEBVTT

NOTE Ruwaidix source-grounded narration; original owner archive and labeled explanations.

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.819
In 2016, we met around an organic chemistry bench.

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:05.335
Myrrh,

00:00:05.335 --> 00:00:09.188
nutmeg, extraction questions, and the suspicion that a

00:00:09.188 --> 00:00:12.321
traditional medicinal claim needed more than an

00:00:12.321 --> 00:00:13.521
interesting smell.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.959
It was easy to obtain an extract and much harder to

00:00:20.959 --> 00:00:21.917
say what it

00:00:21.917 --> 00:00:24.538
contained. Identifying a constituent would still be

00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:25.001
different

00:00:25.001 --> 00:00:27.314
from proving a useful biological effect.

00:00:29.978 --> 00:00:33.162
The group that became Chem Squad included seven

00:00:33.162 --> 00:00:33.772
chemistry

00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:37.487
graduates. There was no grand institution behind us.

00:00:37.487 --> 00:00:37.987
We kept

00:00:37.987 --> 00:00:41.178
bringing papers, arguments, and new questions back to

00:00:41.178 --> 00:00:42.202
the conversation.

00:00:45.103 --> 00:00:48.089
Around that period, our student chapter of the

00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:49.193
American Chemical

00:00:49.193 --> 00:00:52.798
Society at Qatar University was creating a different

00:00:52.798 --> 00:00:53.283
kind of

00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:56.964
laboratory: one open to more students and the public.

00:00:59.812 --> 00:01:02.348
We organized demonstrations and scientific

00:01:02.348 --> 00:01:03.556
discussions. Through

00:01:03.556 --> 00:01:06.302
chapter activities, twenty-nine students had

00:01:06.302 --> 00:01:07.300
opportunities to

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.246
train on instruments. The work was collective; the

00:01:11.246 --> 00:01:12.114
photographs

00:01:12.114 --> 00:01:13.719
deserve collective credit.

00:01:16.853 --> 00:01:19.533
Chemistry festivals taught me another form of

00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:20.128
precision:

00:01:20.128 --> 00:01:23.694
speaking clearly when the audience has every reason to

00:01:23.694 --> 00:01:24.222
question

00:01:24.222 --> 00:01:27.650
you, and resisting the urge to make a demonstration

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:28.725
seem conclusive.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.080
As years passed, we moved into different specialties.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:35.349
Some

00:01:35.349 --> 00:01:38.115
conversations continued through weekly meetings, and

00:01:38.115 --> 00:01:38.328
some

00:01:38.328 --> 00:01:42.266
through disagreements sent across a phone long after a

00:01:42.266 --> 00:01:43.433
class had ended.

00:01:46.228 --> 00:01:50.167
There is no final group photograph that explains all

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.000
of it. What

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.763
the archive shows is simpler: people kept making time

00:01:54.763 --> 00:01:54.976
for

00:01:54.976 --> 00:01:57.759
scientific curiosity, even when nobody assigned it.
